                    "Digiday spoke to <mark>18 media buyers</mark> and found clients putting Google through the kind of scrutiny usually reserved for newer channels.  Lindsay Marty, founder of Above the Bar Marketing, said the amount being questioned is generally around <mark>10 to 20 percent</mark> of the Google budget when the conversation comes up.  Bryce Hamlin, vice president of data intelligence at Power Digital, put it at <mark>10 to 30 percent</mark> of the search budget getting reallocated.  Accuracast group chief executive Farhad Divecha said about 10 percent for now, rising to 20 or 30 percent quite rapidly given the pressure around Black Friday.",
