                    "The numbers.  Across his last ten uploads, 6 September to 31 October, the <mark>median is 52,268 views</mark>, from a middle pair of 51,197 and 53,339.  Across the previous ten, roughly July to late August, the <mark>median is 23,940</mark>, from a middle pair of 23,301 and 24,579.  That is <mark>2.18 times</mark>.  The median is the right measure here because the recent block contains a 160,573 outlier that would flatter an average, and the floor moved too: his weakest recent video did 29,271, which beats six of the previous ten.",
                    "The turn is datable to the day, because he published it.  On <mark>22 August</mark> he uploaded a four-minute video called Changes are Coming to the Channel, in which he says it is time to switch things up, that he is getting back to his roots by visiting food producers and exploring new types of content beyond the regular Old Cookbook Show formula, and that regular programming will return by late September or early October.  The two weeks before that video are the trough of the whole year: four uploads about aviation and charity flights, doing between 7,776 and 14,327 views, a fifth of his normal.",
                    "Three things changed and they are all checkable.  First, the aviation material has gone to a second channel, Glens Hangar, and not one aviation video has appeared on the cooking feed since 26 August.  Second, from 6 September the cadence became regular, roughly one upload every six days, and the subject narrowed to food only.  Third, and this is the one nobody notices, the descriptions were rebuilt.  His 26 August upload has no description body at all.  His 31 October upload has timestamped chapters, a written frequently-asked-questions block, a full ingredient list in both metric and imperial, and four internal links to related videos.  Every upload since early September follows that template.",
