                    "The brand this channel suits is a legacy packaged-food company with an archive: condensed milk, flour, spices, baking, the companies that printed promotional recipe booklets for fifty years.  And the thing to buy is not a read, it is the format he is already making for free.  His 31 October video is a 1931 promotional pie recipe from a condensed-milk brand, with the brand's history told on camera, and it did 160,573 views in three days with no money involved.  The buy is a four to six episode run of the Old Cookbook Show built from one brand's own historical cookbooks and calendars, where the brand supplies the archive and the product and Glen and Julie rule on whether the recipe survives contact with 2026.  The honest answer has to be allowed, in writing, in a clause that gives the brand no veto over the result, because the verdict is the format.  A cookware or appliance brand has an easier second buy: he uses a forty-year-old food processor on camera and never names it.",
